From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: luoye-cpu <3412829159@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:30:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] avfilter/vf_libvmaf: copy all planes of CUDA hardware frames

copy_picture_data_cuda() loops over the planes of the source pixel format
but breaks out after the first cuMemcpy2D(), so only the luma plane is
copied into the VmafPicture. Chroma-based features then read zeroed
memory: with feature=name=speed_chroma the pooled speed_chroma_uv score
is 0 on the CUDA path while the CPU path reports about 19.65 for the same
input, measured against upstream libvmaf.

The accepted formats are fully planar, with one component per plane.
Therefore, iterating over nb_components copies all planes for the formats
supported by this filter.

Depends on the error-path series ("avfilter/vf_libvmaf: fix error paths",
hunk context builds on; the two series touch adjacent lines of the same
loop.

Signed-off-by: luoye-cpu <3412829159@qq.com>
---
 libavfilter/vf_libvmaf.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavfilter/vf_libvmaf.c b/libavfilter/vf_libvmaf.c
index 6400168f40b764599a57053b15d0685f809b7e6f..72145d2df5bc11b06377dcd9e1c0c0939b28dfac 100644
--- a/libavfilter/vf_libvmaf.c
+++ b/libavfilter/vf_libvmaf.c
@@ -752,7 +752,6 @@ static int copy_picture_data_cuda(VmafContext* vmaf,
         err = cu->cuMemcpy2D(&m);
         if (err)
             return AVERROR_EXTERNAL;
-        break;
     }
 
     err = cu->cuCtxPopCurrent(NULL);
